// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//
// Plain-English overview: federal income tax withholding, computed the way
// IRS Publication 15-T tells an automated payroll system to: Worksheet 1A
// plus the Annual Percentage Method tables. It replaces the old flat 12%
// placeholder.
//
// The bracket tables below were generated by tools/pub15t/generate_brackets.py
// from the IRS's own
// publications (2026: the irs.gov HTML edition of Pub 15-T; 2025: the
// Pub 15-T (2025) PDF), not typed by hand, and test/federalWithholding.test.js
// checks every bracket's base amount against the bracket before it, so a
// corrupted number fails CI. Like irsLimits.js, a year with no table
// throws: payroll never withholds using another year's brackets.
//
// Amounts are integer cents; rates are basis points (1200 = 12%).
// Each bracket row is [overCents, baseCents, rateBp]: if the adjusted
// annual wage is at least overCents (column A), the annual tentative
// withholding is baseCents (column C) plus rateBp of the excess (column D).
//
// Not covered here: state and local income tax (see payrollEngine.js),
// supplemental-wage flat rates (bonuses), and nonresident-alien
// adjustments (Pub 15-T section 1, Table 2).

